@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# Post-It's functions
+
+Step 4 of the Post-It plan, phase A: the functions Post-It calls in place of its Apps Script, in
+`firebase/functions/src/posting/`. Tests: `firebase/tests/posting.test.ts`, on the emulator.
+
+Not built yet: phase B (Post-It signs in here and calls these) and phase C (listings through Post-It's Apps
+Script with a secret, the copy of each post in the posting tracker sheet, and the import of the sheet's history).
+
+## Data
+
+| Collection | One document per | Fields |
+|---|---|---|
+| `posts` | post logged | folderId, title, type, fbAccount, link, status (Posted, Pending), by (uid), byName, loggedBy (an admin's uid, when they logged it for someone), date (Manila, yyyy-MM-dd), time (HH:mm), at, sheetCopied |
+| `assignments` | listing in a queue | week (its Monday), assignedTo (uid), assignedToName, folderId, name, order, status (Not Shared, Pending, Posted), by, at |
+| `cooldowns` | listing, by folder ID | last (the day it was last posted), post |
+| `config/posting` | the one document | cooldownDays (7), repostDueDays (14), perWeek (40) |
+| `users` | person | adds `fbProfiles: [{ account, link }]`: the FB accounts they post as, each with its profile link |
+
+Missed is worked out, never saved: an open item of a week that's over.
+
+## Functions
+
+Who: **people** is owner, admin and agent; **managers** is owner and admin. The scanner and an account with no role
+get nothing. A refusal's `details.error` names it, as Post-It's Apps Script replies did.
+
+| Function | Who | Does |
+|---|---|---|
+| `postingStart` | people | `{ rules, today, week, me: { uid, name, role, fbProfiles } }` |
+| `listPosts` `{ from? }` | people | Posts, oldest first. An agent gets their own |
+| `listAssignments` `{ week? }` | people | Queue items by week, agent and order. An agent gets their own |
+| `logPost` `{ folderId, title, type?, fbAccount, link, status, postedBy? }` | people | Refuses `link-required`, `bad-link`, `bad-status`, `forbidden` (not one of the poster's FB accounts), `cooldown` (with `lastPosted`, `nextAllowed`). A manager may log for an active person with `postedBy` (uid). Moves the poster's open queue item for the listing to the post's status |
+| `addLink` `{ postId, link }` | people | A Pending post made Posted, with its live link. An agent's own only |
+| `setStatus` `{ assignmentId, status }` | people | A queue item moved. Posted also makes the assignee's newest Pending post of it Posted. An agent's own only |
+| `saveQueues` `{ week, queues: [{ assignedTo, items: [{ folderId, name, status? }] }] }` | managers | Replaces those agents' items of that week, all or nothing. Refuses `bad-week`, `bad-queues`, `bad-agent`, and `held` (with `held: [{ folderId, name, heldBy, heldByName, week }]`) |
+| `setRules` `{ cooldownDays?, repostDueDays?, perWeek? }` | managers | Only what's sent changes. `bad-rules` (with `field`) |
+| `setFbProfiles` `{ uid, fbProfiles }` | managers | An owner anyone's, an admin an agent's, and anyone their own. `bad-accounts`, `bad-profile-link` |
+
+`listPeople` also returns each person's `fbProfiles`.
+
+## How the rules hold
+
+- **The cooldown** reads one document, `cooldowns/{folderId}`, and writes it with the post, in one transaction: two
+  people logging the same listing at once can't both get through (a test sends two at the same moment).
+- **The held rule** reads the open items of weeks that aren't over (`status == Not Shared`, `week >= this week`) in the
+  same transaction as the save.
+- **Logging and changes check the account now** (`requireCurrentRole`): a turned-off agent is refused at once.
+- **Days are Manila's** (UTC+8, no daylight saving), as in Post-It.
+
+Two composite indexes, in `firestore.indexes.json`: assignments by status and week, and posts by poster and date.
